1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,716
Documentation written from the code, not from memory.

2
00:00:03,766 --> 00:00:06,985
With workdocs you type one command: /workdocs.

3
00:00:07,035 --> 00:00:12,315
The agent reads the manifest, the entry points, the handlers and the tests,

4
00:00:12,365 --> 00:00:18,497
then writes six pages: Overview, Setup, How it works, Security, API, and a demo script.

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,776
The result is plain static HTML in your docs folder.

6
00:00:21,826 --> 00:00:25,924
Each section names the files it came from; mocked parts are labelled.

7
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:32,837
How it works shows the real calls as an animated flow, and walks one request through a sequence diagram on its own.

8
00:00:32,887 --> 00:00:36,565
Nothing to click, nothing to fetch. It even opens from a file.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,791
workdocs. Free.

10
00:00:37,841 --> 00:00:42,650
It pairs with workmap, so documentation and progress read as one site.
